    <!--
        Android re-tints this to a single system color for Material You "themed icons" - a solid
        recolor of the full multi-tone foreground would just merge every shape into one blob with
        no visible structure. Mirrors the full-color mark's own two-tone split instead of
        inventing a new visual language: ink (case/arm/hub) and gold (the wink) are the "solid"
        tones there, while pine (platter/screws) is really just a second surface - so here the
        case is one solid shape with the platter and the four screws punched out as real
        transparent holes (evenOdd fill combining all of them in one path), and the arm/hub/wink
        stay solid on top, floating in the cutout. The source color used here doesn't matter - the
        OS overrides it - #000000 is just convention.
    -->
